title op3: an inner belief is what carries the outer one

# VD7, and the deliberate twin of op3-nested-recreated.  That fixture
# blocks the inner belief and therefore never lets a directory child
# vote at all; this one lets the inner belief succeed, so the fourth
# row of the vote triad -- a directory child accounted for by a
# believed move OF ITS OWN -- is the only thing holding the outer
# move up.
#
# Off-of rebuilds /top as /peak and, inside it, /top/inner as
# /peak/core.  Both directories are severed; the file underneath
# keeps its dnode.  Onto is quiet.
#
# PHASE 2 RUNS BOTTOM-UP BY HEIGHT, and here the order is load
# bearing rather than decorative.
#
#   height 0: f's red edge nominates (base /top/inner, /peak/core),
#     and it is the only candidate -- there is no rival for the
#     sibling generator to find, which is the single difference from
#     op3-nested-recreated.  f votes by red, unanimously, into a
#     unique target.  /top/inner is BELIEVED to have moved to
#     /peak/core.
#
#   height 1: /top's only child is the directory inner.  Red is dead
#     for it.  Yellow is not available to a directory at all.  A NAME
#     MATCH FAILS TOO, deliberately -- the leaf is inner on one side
#     and core on the other, so the row that rescued the directory
#     child in op3-dir-yellow-abstain cannot rescue this one.  What
#     is left is the fourth row: inner has a believed move, and its
#     target sits inside /peak, so it votes there.  /top is BELIEVED
#     to have moved to /peak.
#
# Reverse the order and nothing works: at height 1 the inner belief
# would not exist yet, /top would have no voter, and fullness would
# be vacuous.  Proposition 16.4's induction is well founded precisely
# because a directory's vote as a child was decided at a strictly
# smaller height, and this is the smallest fixture where that
# sentence does any work.
#
# The two leaf names differ on purpose.  If core were called inner,
# the name-match row would carry the vote and the fourth row would
# never be reached -- which is exactly how this cell stayed empty
# through the first sixteen fixtures.
#
# WORKED OUTCOME (by hand, before any implementation ran)
#   believed moves:  /top/inner -> /peak/core at height 0, on f's red
#                    vote; then /top -> /peak at height 1, on inner's
#                    believed move and nothing else
#   deltas:          none.  Relative to the believed pairs every leaf
#                    is unchanged
#   decisions:       /peak reuses onto's dnode 2, /peak/core reuses
#                    dnode 3, f keeps dnode 4.  With the inner belief
#                    refused, all three would materialize
#   conflicts:       none, onto is quiet
#   emission:        rename top to peak in the root's scope, then
#                    rename inner to core inside it, ordered after by
#                    the parent-first arrow.  f needs no edit: its
#                    relativized name never changed

tree base
  1-1: /
    2-100: top/
      3-100: inner/
        4-100: f = fv0

tree onto
  1-1: /
    2-100: top/
      3-100: inner/
        4-100: f = fv0

tree offof
  1-1: /
    20-300: peak/
      30-300: core/
        4-100: f = fv0

# --- expected result, worked by hand 2026-08-31 ---
expect clean

tree expected
  1-1: /
    2-100: peak
      3-100: core
        4-100: f = fv0
